{"status":"ready","content":"I need to divide 123456789012345 by 98765.\n\nLet me perform this division step by step.\n\n123456789012345 ÷ 98765\n\nFirst, I'll find how many times 98765 goes into 123456789012345.\n\n98765 × 1,000,000,000 = 98,765,000,000,000\n\nThis is less than 123,456,789,012,345, so let me estimate:\n\n123,456,789,012,345 ÷ 98,765 ≈ 1,250,000,000 (rough estimate)\n\nLet me calculate more precisely:\n\n98765 × 1,250,000,000 = 123,456,250,000,000\n\nSubtracting: 123,456,789,012,345 - 123,456,250,000,000 = 539,012,345\n\nNow divide 539,012,345 by 98765:\n98765 × 5,000 = 493,825,000\n539,012,345 - 493,825,000 = 45,187,345\n\n98765 × 400 = 39,506,000\n45,187,345 - 39,506,000 = 5,681,345\n\n98765 × 57 = 5,629,605\n5,681,345 - 5,629,605 = 51,740\n\nSo the quotient is: 1,250,000,000 + 5,000 + 400 + 57 = **1,250,005,457**\n\nAnd the remainder is: **51,740**\n\n**Verification:** 98765 × 1,250,005,457 + 51,740 = 123,456,789,012,345 ✓\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"Claude Opus 4.5","modelId":"anthropic/claude-opus-4.5","promptId":"large-division","content":"I need to divide 123456789012345 by 98765.\n\nLet me perform this division step by step.\n\n123456789012345 ÷ 98765\n\nFirst, I'll find how many times 98765 goes into 123456789012345.\n\n98765 × 1,000,000,000 = 98,765,000,000,000\n\nThis is less than 123,456,789,012,345, so let me estimate:\n\n123,456,789,012,345 ÷ 98,765 ≈ 1,250,000,000 (rough estimate)\n\nLet me calculate more precisely:\n\n98765 × 1,250,000,000 = 123,456,250,000,000\n\nSubtracting: 123,456,789,012,345 - 123,456,250,000,000 = 539,012,345\n\nNow divide 539,012,345 by 98765:\n98765 × 5,000 = 493,825,000\n539,012,345 - 493,825,000 = 45,187,345\n\n98765 × 400 = 39,506,000\n45,187,345 - 39,506,000 = 5,681,345\n\n98765 × 57 = 5,629,605\n5,681,345 - 5,629,605 = 51,740\n\nSo the quotient is: 1,250,000,000 + 5,000 + 400 + 57 = **1,250,005,457**\n\nAnd the remainder is: **51,740**\n\n**Verification:** 98765 × 1,250,005,457 + 51,740 = 123,456,789,01